SET Support = "The infection of SARS virus is initiated by the attachment of S protein to the receptor ACE2 [19], followed by cleavage with host cell protease TMPRSS2 [20-22]. The viruses are then transported through the early and late endosomes, subsequently endo/lysosomes, during which host protein extracellular proteases including cathepsin L mediates the further cleavage of S protein in endocytic vesicles [23-26]. The activated S protein will then activate the fusion between viral and cell membranes and release the genome of SARS-CoV into cytoplasm."
